# REGRESSION (was todo/t0840): the CONTAINER axis — `Dict[K, Shared[V]]`.
# `gorget_map_put`'s value parameter carries the same `AbiKind::VoidElem` tag
# as `gorget_array_push`'s element, so the Dict cell died identically (rc 139,
# both backends) and is fixed by the same shared dispatcher.
#
# `Set[Shared[T]]` is the one container cell that is NOT covered here and never
# will be: `Shared[int]` does not satisfy `Hashable`, so a Set of handles is a
# check-time REJECT (`E_UnsatisfiedTraitBound`), not a lowering path.
#
# ⚠ The key/value ITERATION over the same Dict is deliberately NOT here, and
# this is a recorded gap, not a dodge: `for (k, v) in d` over refcount VALUES
# over-releases (`AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free` inside
# `gorget_map_free`), while the identical loop over `String` values is clean.
# That is refcount ARITHMETIC at the iteration bind, not the marshalling class
# this cell pins, and it ships as its own `#[ignore]`d cell,
# `shared_dict_iteration_value_over_release.gg` (todo/t0907).
#
# CELL: container=Dict(value) · handle=Shared · payload=int ·
#       producing-arm=put · read=`.get(k).unwrap()`.

void main():
    Shared[int] s = Shared[int](11)
    Dict[String, Shared[int]] d = {}
    d.put("a", s.clone())
    d.put("b", s.clone())
    print(f"{d.len()}")
    print(f"{d.get('a').unwrap().get()}")
    print(f"{s.strong_count()}")
